{#
  module/SionModel/view/sion-model/sion-model/view-changes.phtml, ported.

  The .phtml is four lines: a headTitle, an <h1>, and a partial. The <h1> says
  "Database edits" while the page title says "View Changes" — reproduced rather than
  reconciled, because a port is not the place to decide which one is right.

  The table itself is _changes-table.html.twig, kept separate for the same reason the
  original keeps `changes-table` a partial: SionModel renders it from more than one place
  (an entity's own change panel), so the next port to need it should extend this file's
  include rather than copy the table.
#}
{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block content %}
<h1>{{ translate('Database edits') }}</h1>
{% include 'sion-model/_changes-table.html.twig' with {
    'changes': changes,
    'max_rows': max_rows,
    'show_entity': show_entity,
} only %}
{% endblock %}
